    <worksheet name='Q2( Depth and Mag of EQ)'>
      <layout-options>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Interpretation</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Observing the scatter plot, we can observe that:</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*Most earthquakes have a </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>magnitude between 7 and 8</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*Most earthquakes occur at </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>shallow to medium depths</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*The trend line slopes slightly upward. This means </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>deeper earthquakes tend to have    slightly higher magnitudes</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*The relationship is </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>weak</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>, so depth does not strongly determine earthquake magnitude. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*There are a few </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>very large earthquakes (above magnitude 8)</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>, but they are rare. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>*Overall, the chart shows </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>no strong correlation between earthquake depth and magnitude</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='query (Mag6PlusEarthquakes)' name='federated.1pbaolm1ftsmh215b5gw519op2cx' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.1pbaolm1ftsmh215b5gw519op2cx'>
            <column caption='Depth' datatype='real' name='[depth]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column caption='Mag' datatype='real' name='[mag]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[depth]' derivation='None' name='[none:depth:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
